# oracle: pouring spheres above a plane of triangles read from an STL file by fix surface/global input stl, turned about z (in.tribox.gran.global.stl cut down: 30 spheres poured, 1000 steps in one run; 3d, STL input, the example's surf.tri.stl)
# oracle-note: in.tribox.gran.global.stl reads surf.tri.stl (the 4-triangle plane), not surf.tribox.stl; the case follows the example. One run of 1000 steps: a second run while fix pour is still inserting makes native insert a sphere at the first step of the run, which the engine does not (fix pour, not the surface; see the report).
# oracle-inputs: w127gsg_surf.tri.stl
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# oracle-measured: max relative error (native fixture vs engine, scale max(1,|LAMMPS|)): thermo 1.3e-14, per-atom 1.8e-13 (measured with tests/fixtures/oracle, 2026-10-13)
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
boundary        f f f
dimension       3
comm_modify     vel yes

region          box block -10 10 -10 10 -10 10 units box
create_box      2 box

pair_style      granular
pair_coeff      * * hooke 4000.0 100.0 &
                    tangential linear_history 1000.0 1.0 0.5 &
                    damping mass_velocity

neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes

fix             20 all surface/global input stl 2 1 w127gsg_surf.tri.stl &
                model * * granular hooke 4000.0 100.0 &
                    tangential linear_history 1000.0 1.0 0.5 &
                    damping mass_velocity

fix             2 all nve/sphere
fix             3 all gravity 1.0 vector 0 0 -1

region          slab block -2 2 -2 2 -2 2 units box
fix             ins all pour 30 1 4767548 vol 0.4 10 &
                diam one 1.0 region slab ignore

timestep        0.005

compute         1 all temp
compute_modify  1 dynamic/dof yes

compute         2 all temp/sphere
compute_modify  2 dynamic/dof yes

thermo_style    custom step atoms temp c_1 c_2 press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g lost ignore
compute_modify  thermo_temp dynamic/dof yes
thermo          100

fix_modify      20 move * rotate 0 0 0 0 0 1 25
run             1000
